# Netlify redirects. Must sit in the published directory root.
#
# The v1 site renamed three pages that are indexed today. Without these, those
# URLs 404 on launch and lose whatever ranking and inbound links they carry.
# Both forms are listed because the old site linked with .html and Netlify also
# serves the extensionless form, so Google may have either.
#
# 301 = permanent, which is what passes ranking. Do not use 302 here.

/forestry-and-milling.html            /forest-management.html    301
/forestry-and-milling                 /forest-management.html    301

/manufacturing-and-distribution.html  /wood-products.html        301
/manufacturing-and-distribution       /wood-products.html        301

/learn-more.html                      /how-it-works.html         301
/learn-more                           /how-it-works.html         301

# forestry-and-milling split into forest-management and sawmills. It points at
# forest-management because that is the closer match to the old page's content;
# the nav gets the reader to sawmills in one click from there.
